module main

import std.io

"Hello, world!" print_str new_line


include "cores/select.cal"
include "std/io.cal"

"Hello, world!\n" print_str


Output:
Hello, world!


How it works:
- include "cores/select.cal" – Selects the appropriate platform core.
- include "std/io.cal" – Imports standard input/output functions.
- "Hello, world!\n" – Pushes a string onto the stack.
- print_str – Prints the string to the console.
